{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And I shall lie with my fathers.</b> This vav is connected back to the beginning of the verse — 'Place your hand under my thigh and swear to me' — and I am destined to lie with my fathers, and you shall carry me out of Egypt. One should not say, 'and I shall lie with my fathers' — bury me with my fathers in the cave, for afterward it is written, 'and you shall carry me out of Egypt and bury me in their burial-place.' Moreover, we find everywhere that the expression 'lying with his fathers' is the dying, not the burial, as in 'David lay with his fathers,' and afterward 'and he was buried in the City of David' (I Kings 2)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:03:53.161637693Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}